                    <nc xml:id="m-0753a714-0eb5-4222-b102-2feaea4344ba" pname="c" oct="4" />
                    <nc xml:id="m-1b8b9550-5fb2-4a20-87c0-57dd6b1e982a" pname="b" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <syllable xml:id="m-0cbc4aaa-b4bc-4ae9-98cc-033c9402352f">
                  <syl /><neume facs="#m-7b2ac90b-0d9b-4cd4-b494-26a5380ee537" type="clivis" xml:id="m-e6e8fe8d-8626-400e-a3cc-e6f01445aaaa">
                    <nc xml:id="m-c45d9403-5288-4e0d-9d98-fbceea5706ba" pname="a" oct="3" />
                    <nc xml:id="m-48611fcf-b903-4f04-9e5d-f17831408a51" pname="g" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <syllable xml:id="m-5416d865-29e7-4c1d-8827-f35b5132c901">
                  <syl /><neume facs="#m-fffbb026-3501-47bf-b1b8-e8d9ca5424f4" type="punctum" xml:id="m-3a9f5a62-8dbb-46de-9b39-7df27e66d6f5">
                    <nc xml:id="m-676c78fe-f6f3-43de-b549-16fd276ea006" pname="a" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <syllable xml:id="m-e56f8a9b-ecee-41a1-9357-52bf637dd837">
                  <syl /><neume facs="#m-35b2b712-ba90-4b0f-aa8a-113564c2817c" type="punctum" xml:id="m-2f3d3ca9-b0ba-4a32-bac2-6d0c56b5936e">
                    <nc xml:id="m-3344955a-0473-4366-869d-63f996ae99c9" pname="b" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <syllable xml:id="m-434076eb-1982-4f4c-8839-31299ad56d3e">
                  <syl /><neume facs="#m-206e4ba1-e2ca-4bac-a631-0218b14c6926" type="podatus" xml:id="m-be422421-5df1-4b97-82c7-affbfa2c5ffc">
                    <nc xml:id="m-d13053b2-abcf-4a3c-9124-0653c03a4a2c" pname="g" oct="3" />
                    <nc xml:id="m-68982871-34d6-42e8-a8e7-f29279d941b4" pname="a" oct="3" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <divLine xml:id="m-55c10a83-e3d4-41d8-b0d7-73c5225dbd65" facs="#m-57bb556c-2330-40aa-89c0-b292c131335d" form="finalis" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-9d060275-02cc-4965-8c6a-466d2f3b31af">
              <lg xml:id="m-3ba7446c-ae41-4b98-8dca-a4b1ce4a3d80">
                <l xml:id="m-b363c96a-a17f-4755-8563-f9831a696d34" facs="#m-a9573eb5-b99c-4ec9-a2ec-86a178aafbb7" label="text-like">The Solemn evening Mass</l><l xml:id="m-e9c73466-1699-4c06-897a-4da1e2699bfa" facs="#m-a520d730-68ff-4e61-9e90-c7e397e9ec59" label="ambiguous">e71</l><l xml:id="m-5e0453ec-29dc-4131-8e23-7f19064dec04" facs="#m-2b9ab107-2c3b-4baa-a45a-e8df6fe47173" label="text-like">THE WASHING OF THE FEET</l><l xml:id="m-7b174bb0-0b00-4180-95b8-737b29ebea9f" facs="#m-3e2a2ac3-314b-4ae3-bcb0-9c5d43e4981c" label="text-like">15. Where it is desirable for pastoral reasons, the Washing of the feet</l><l xml:id="m-236f69ed-b0ca-4147-8835-ebbd73bf5e34" facs="#m-1324c64b-9103-4fb6-8c38-3aa893199f06" label="text-like">tahes place after the sermon.</l><l xml:id="m-3587a893-ebe2-44cd-9358-c148d78823ee" facs="#m-195348a2-4678-4d3c-9269-8096ecab8f2b" label="text-like">16. In the sanctuary or the nave, benches are prepared face to face for the</l><l xml:id="m-ac0423b2-231f-49f9-bd03-54c72965235b" facs="#m-e57beaba-a9b9-43f3-9e0f-e30d7b88174c" label="ambiguous">relve men whose feet will be washed : everythine necessary uill be prepared</l><l xml:id="m-fc43af86-8d90-42fc-922d-009fd0e7d624" facs="#m-69f7cad3-3b10-4a7d-adba-e075681b6648" label="text-like">on a table at a suitable time.</l><l xml:id="m-7c3b7954-8f7e-4a75-9d1d-a42f1fe77ab4" facs="#m-1fe3a877-8306-46e3-ba10-4b55c6ec1d2c" label="text-like">17. The celebrant, having made reverence to the altar, goes to the bench and</l><l xml:id="m-5b770693-9ea0-4668-9a52-0acaf70a7802" facs="#m-32b3f71f-848c-4e73-b2dd-8d28093549df" label="text-like">sits. The deacon and subdeacon Ior the tuo principal servers] brinɇ the</l><l xml:id="m-b591cad4-6803-4c6d-9e98-7f882b5b15f9" facs="#m-bc9aa0b3-4ab4-4fff-a69f-47b817be09a3" label="text-like">tuelve men two by two to the place prepared for them, during which time</l><l xml:id="m-18792634-4e6c-46d8-9e4a-c8edab5d5b6d" facs="#m-bdf8e36e-1340-48e7-86cc-a201835ce6a9" label="text-like">the schola or the clergy begin io sing or recite the antiphons, psalms and</l><l xml:id="m-541d4bd2-2995-44f5-939d-9a1a3b69aa67" facs="#m-cbb6afa7-8299-4257-bc40-2e813fa97954" label="ambiguous">verses indicated belouo.</l><l xml:id="m-f8b84fe8-74db-4833-b167-b99178262cf9" facs="#m-33878f09-7501-40d3-bccd-dfe1a9dba1af" label="text-like">The tuelve men who are chosen, having genuflected to the altar and boued</l><l xml:id="m-472a4210-aba3-42dd-870f-74660600c1f5" facs="#m-bfeffe20-ca3c-4378-b4db-1d9f1aeb6966" label="text-like">to the celebrant sitting in the sanctuary, tahe their places on the seats prepared;</l><l xml:id="m-d7db6839-abd4-4afc-8a08-4b4c8c5e3169" facs="#m-99d9fb75-ffc7-48bd-ad0d-aa9c96134abe" label="text-like">the sacred ministers for serversl help the celebrant. Al ae off their maniples,</l><l xml:id="m-e9cd4095-d805-4dc8-8af0-bba04d85a95c" facs="#m-93855ee0-8e27-45ac-b1a9-c286201e88ab" label="text-like">and the celebrant his chasuble, putting a touel around his waist.</l><l xml:id="m-82fc1279-90f7-4bce-bc1e-f1c58465e40b" facs="#m-30e355e8-3985-40a2-a7c7-8b88951dd3ca" label="text-like">18. The celebrant goes to the middle with the ministers Ior serversl, mahes</l><l xml:id="m-00905acf-bf28-4fcc-b7c4-22c6a0a386ee" facs="#m-3ec0684c-7f5b-44c4-ac22-7bcdf2f6ce01" label="text-like">reverence to the altar, and begins the feet-zvashing as follozos. He hneels</l><l xml:id="m-6973f957-835b-46aa-bcc5-e59091fe3c15" facs="#m-d3521f48-7674-4ffe-b739-b32bd3aaa12a" label="text-like">before each one, the subdeacon lor second serverl holds the right foot, while</l><l xml:id="m-fc8ff048-6411-4619-a04f-00f446b4806f" facs="#m-d500f142-a6e0-4aeb-b306-2ee6bf5c132e" label="text-like">acolytes lIor two other serversl have ready water and basin; he washes the</l><l xml:id="m-5d367cf9-310f-4bd8-8c60-22a9927cc3c8" facs="#m-08d4d429-e40c-4914-979c-3a56f0730df0" label="text-like">fooi, then dries it, the deacon sor first serverl handine the towvel.</l><l xml:id="m-e63f5b0a-6df9-4240-88b9-dec399f3bae6" facs="#m-3da576b8-5a3b-4836-abdd-3e9a43e2559c" label="lyrics-like">When the washing of the feet is nearly ended, the Sth antiphon Ubi cáritas</l><l xml:id="m-3747da0a-8046-4ff9-b3a4-2c6c743cfa4b" facs="#m-f5127617-3c04-44dd-9c54-28ae8dec1453" label="text-like">vith its verses is begun. I necessary, some of the preceding antiphons may</l><l xml:id="m-1f7701c8-b557-4f32-8b8a-0f61c902ed28" facs="#m-053550b7-9d6e-4b6e-87d7-5dc3af8cb3b4" label="lyrics-like">be omitted, but never this antiphon Ubi cáritas.</l><l xml:id="m-4be86252-f48e-4325-b923-0b27b2f8bf7b" facs="#m-f264d967-f14c-420d-b2cc-c3768931fa14" label="text-like">19. The antiphons, psalms and verses to be sung or recited are these.</l><l xml:id="m-95140dc9-a8f0-499b-8a96-d54fb8641930" facs="#m-f35981c0-55b2-41e3-8694-5563cb998537" label="text-like">ANTIPHON PS. 118, 1</l><l xml:id="m-947a3b41-093c-4403-97bf-4442a85dba04" facs="#m-3430ff63-65ff-4580-8443-3ae2eba4aca4" label="lyrics-like">Andátum nóvum do vóbis:*ut di-ligá-tis invicem,</l><l xml:id="m-22c63f9b-fa41-4fff-afb2-642b41480b6f" facs="#m-b3c03e8d-1e4d-46b7-a900-9ebfc02b005f" label="lyrics-like">sicut di-léxi vos, dí-cit Dóminus. Ps. Be-á-ti immaculá-ti</l><l xml:id="m-4eebd53c-c8c8-4ba7-b248-2c7c695c204e" facs="#m-1c463c2f-e6c5-4b01-b71a-d86fb0c889d6" label="lyrics-like">in v¬:"qui ámbu-lant in lé-ge Dómi-ni.</l><l xml:id="m-47f5f553-f373-47de-9534-96e316aa7b58" facs="#m-85234f1f-e251-424b-9a7b-a66a899e9cb2" label="lyrics-like">The Antiphon Mandátum nóvum. is repeated.</l><l xml:id="m-1e6e39ec-88eb-4fce-82b1-1906349ef845" facs="#m-257063e3-8b48-4222-900d-15eb0318c899" label="text-like">The follouing Antiphons are each repeated after the Psalm or Versicle.</l><l xml:id="m-36d1a501-0f4e-43cd-af8c-2e360acfe657" facs="#m-8da737bc-602c-4b46-83f9-f65538aa03d5" label="text-like">Only the first verse of the Psalm is said in each case.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>